---
description: Charting and data visualization standards
globs: apps/web/**/*Chart*.tsx, apps/web/**/charts/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Library choice
- OHLCV/candles/volumes/overlays: `lightweight-charts` (TradingView).
- Bespoke viz (heatmap, treemap, violin, drawdown, seasonality): `d3` primitives — no d3 React wrappers.

# Performance
- Be careful with resize and rerender behavior; chart containers should respond cleanly to layout changes.
- If datasets become large, prefer server-side aggregation or downsampling over rendering raw data blindly.
- Avoid DOM-heavy chart rendering patterns for large series.

# UX
- Make the distinction between historical and predicted data visually obvious when forecasts are shown.
- Charts should communicate the dataset clearly with labels, legends, or nearby supporting text.
